+# Desert bank blend, bridge continuity and warm road colour
+
+2026-10-13 owner correction. DS18 adopts Winter's settled/granular road-to-bank transition; DS19 lightens the road and reduces wear contrast; DS20 fixes road-to-bridge pattern continuity; DS21 responds to the later rejection of the dull road hue. Preserve V02/V04/V05/G01/R01/Q01, original nine-second desert dust, approved tire-mark colour, low wind-shaped deposits, five laps, local per-car condition and canonical driving/scoring.
+
+Winter's `winter_bank.gdshader` blends a settled deposit and broken fine grains with `shoulder_fringe`, while its actual road retains directional material detail. Desert now uses that same shared fringe, with broad world-space breakup, over a 1.95 m cosmetic foot instead of the earlier 0.93 m strip/approximately 0.28 m interpolation. The foot carries the existing compacted-road texture through the blend into the same loose shoulder material used on the bank. Bank geometry, crown height, fragments and terrain relief are unchanged.
+
+The first lighter but still brown `847357` road was rejected during this task. The final road is restrained golden sand `9f8052`, with shared warm `ad8957` shoulders. Road and loose sand follow the dunes' warm hue; a small value difference and directional wear distinguish compaction. No scene-lighting or camera change is used to conceal the previous palette mismatch. The wear multiplier is reduced from approximately 0.90–1.08 to 0.9475–1.0375, retaining the existing original v3 artwork, mip filtering, connected phase and local junction blend. Intermediate brown and stronger golden captures are retained separately.
+
+Ground road transverse UV is measured with `Vector2.orthogonal()`; bridge geometry uses the opposite transverse basis. The old deck buffer disagreed with the ground by 12 m at a 12 m-wide road's edges, at all four tested headings. Correcting the transverse coordinate before applying the existing phase/sign makes actual deck UV agree with the ground, including reversed spans. A desert-only Burley shader matches ground diffuse lighting. The same settled sand foot continues onto both ramp mouths and recedes over four metres, preventing a texture border along the approach shoulders. Raised bridge geometry, ramps, rails and canonical contacts are retained. Desert bridge shaders receive sampler specialization, including the retained native raster bridge path.
+
+Changed runtime files: `game/track/native_track_visual.gd` (task increments 176→177 and 179→180, concurrent Winter/sand increments retained), `surface_detail.gdshaderinc`, `creator_road.gdshaderinc`, `track_theme.gd`, `creator_bridge_visual.gd`, `bridge_presentation.gd`, `bridge_road.gdshaderinc`, `surface_shader_variants.gd`, and new `desert_bridge_road.gdshader`/UID. New diagnostic: `game/tests/test_desert_bank_bridge_blend.gd`/UID. The existing `profile_desert_reference.gd` receives an optional output-folder argument so historical evidence is preserved. Status, phase plan and agent override are updated. No new artwork, dependency, canonical contract or schema.
+
+Actual commands use `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1` and pinned `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf`:
+
+| Action / arguments | Actual outcome |
+| --- | --- |
+| `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/capture_desert_refinement.gd -Graphical -TestArgument '--evidence-root=res://../docs/evidence/desert-winter-blend-2026-10-13/before'` | Six baseline gameplay/detail/dust views; canonical cells/hash unchanged. |
+| `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_desert_bank_bridge_blend.gd -Graphical -TestArgument '--folder=res://../docs/evidence/desert-winter-blend-2026-10-13/before/bridge/'` | Three baseline detail/approach views; diagnostic logs reproduce the 12 m transverse UV error. Baseline deliberately records the defect; it does not run the corrected-UV assertions. |
+| `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/capture_desert_refinement.gd -Graphical -TestArgument '--evidence-root=res://../docs/evidence/desert-winter-blend-2026-10-13/final-golden'` | Six final Compatibility views; 60,799 bank vertices checked for height, buried toes and road clearance; 184 fragments; canonical cells/hash unchanged. |
+| Same with `-RenderingMethod mobile -RenderingDriver vulkan` and root `final-golden-mobile` | Six final desktop Mobile/Vulkan views; same geometry/canonical checks. |
+| `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_desert_bank_bridge_blend.gd -Graphical -TestArgument '--folder=res://../docs/evidence/desert-winter-blend-2026-10-13/golden-bridge/'` | 656 checks, zero failures: four headings/signs, actual deck UV, bound apron buffers at mouths/core, shader/sampler check, cells/hash and 12 rendered seam samples. Maximum entry/exit RGB delta 0.029607/0.014673, below unchanged 0.035 threshold. |
+| Same with Mobile/Vulkan and folder `golden-mobile-bridge` | 656 checks, zero failures; entry/exit RGB delta 0.031859/0.016169. |
+| `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_desert_crossings.gd -Graphical -TestArgument '--folder=res://../docs/evidence/desert-winter-blend-2026-10-13/golden-crossing/'` | 77 checks, zero failures; single visible 799.442558 m² union, reversed/closed wear phase, local junction blend, 48 camera poses and four pigment-edge samples. |
+| Same with Mobile/Vulkan and folder `golden-mobile-crossing` | 77 checks, zero failures; same coverage/phase/pixel checks. |
+| `TestDesert` | 87 checks, zero failures, including original dust and exact five-car packed/loose-sand replay behavior; repeated after final palette correction. |
+| `TestShoulders` | Union plus 71 visual joins/18 contours, zero failures; canonical contacts/cells retained. |
+| `TestRoadCache` | 70 checks, zero failures. |
+| `TestBridgeContacts` | 16 checks, zero failures. |
+| `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_terrain_sampler_budget.gd` | Final 60 checks, zero failures across five biomes. Earlier 57 reflects the pre-concurrent-bank-specialization material count. Dedicated desert deck also stays within the eight authored-sampler budget. |
+| `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/profile_desert_reference.gd -Graphical -TestArgument '--folder=res://../docs/evidence/desert-winter-blend-2026-10-13/performance/'` | Intermediate brown palette, final blend/UV logic: unscored real AI, 1600×900 RTX 3090, 3 s warmup/8 s measurement, 2,331 frames/960 ticks/22.77 m. Frame median 3.209 ms/p95 4.921/max 28.551. GPU median 0.833/p95 3.220 ms, but a 2,895 ms maximum query outlier prevents a clean GPU-tail claim. Diagnostic is retained; no incremental-cost, final-palette or sustained-phone benchmark is claimed. |
+| `Doctor` | Matching engine/templates; DN2103 attached. Initial sandbox ADB failed to create its Android directory; permitted retry passed. Device availability is not a physical-device test. |
+
+Inspected final [gameplay](evidence/desert-winter-blend-2026-10-13/final-golden/after/route-35.png), [bank detail](evidence/desert-winter-blend-2026-10-13/final-golden/after/bank-detail.png), [Compatibility approach](evidence/desert-winter-blend-2026-10-13/golden-bridge/entry.png) and [Mobile approach](evidence/desert-winter-blend-2026-10-13/golden-mobile-bridge/entry.png). Both final gameplay folders contain original-dust views; both final crossing folders contain 24 moving-camera frames. Intermediate captures and actual dev-command logs are retained.
+
+`preserved-presentation.json` proves the dust, skid-trail and bank-geometry files are byte-for-byte unchanged for this slice; the original desert cloud/profile/alpha/growth/configuration/emitter hashes also still match the earlier pre-refinement source. Concurrent Winter bank specialization and general sand-mineral changes remain in the live workspace and are excluded from the desert-only checkpoint diff.
+
+Reviewable task-only baseline/fix repository: `build/desert_winter_blend/checkpoint-repo`; patch/ledger: `docs/evidence/desert-winter-blend-2026-10-13/task-only.patch` and `checkpoint.json`. The main branch/index is not staged or committed by this task. No Android export/install/device run, backend operation, live account write, production deployment, full Validate or physics merge. Physical-phone appearance/performance/thermal testing was not performed despite the attached device. Remaining acceptance: owner colour/reference review, the owner's exact pictured document (the saved gameplay capture is a different local track), angled/multi-way/painted bridge approaches and narrow islands, plus physical-device quality/performance. AAA remains an owner/device quality target.
